              "version": "3.1"
            },
            "format": "CVSS"
          }
        ],
        "descriptions": [
          {
            "lang": "en",
            "value": "A flaw was found in RESTEasy's IIOImageProvider, which decodes attacker-supplied image request bodies without enforcing any limit on the declared image dimensions or pixel count. A remote, unauthenticated attacker can send a small crafted image declaring enormous dimensions to trigger a very large memory allocation, exhausting the JVM heap and resulting in a denial of service."
          }
        ],
